# {{APP_MODULE}} backend

Generated from the OlegShevtsov1/1_mvp_sdlc project templates at {{SDLC_VERSION}}.

The backend (be) repository of the `{{PROJECT_NAME}}` project: a Rails 7.2 API (Ruby 3.3.6, PostgreSQL 16,
Redis 7) with the process, deploy and observability scaffolding already in place and no business code yet. The
frontend is `{{REPO_FE}}`. Conventions, hard rules and the feature workflow are in `CLAUDE.md`; read it first.

`config/project.env` holds the project identity (`PROJECT_NAME`, `PROJECT_ZONE`); the Kamal configs, the deploy
scripts and the workflows read it. The app answers on `https://{{PROJECT_ZONE}}` (prod) and
`https://dev.{{PROJECT_ZONE}}` (dev).

## Local setup

1. Ruby 3.3.6 (`.ruby-version`), PostgreSQL and Redis running locally.
2. `bin/setup` (installs gems, prepares the database, sets `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`).
   Or by hand: `bundle install`, `bin/rails db:create db:schema:load`, `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.
3. `bin/rails server -p 3000`; `GET http://localhost:3000/health` answers `{"status":"ok",...}` and the API docs
   are at `http://localhost:3000/api-docs`.

`DATABASE_URL` and `REDIS_URL` override the defaults of `config/database.yml` and `config/environments/*.rb`.

## Commands

- Tests: `bundle exec rspec`
- Lint: `bundle exec rubocop --parallel`
- Security: `bundle exec brakeman --no-pager -q`; `bundle exec bundler-audit check --update`
- Dev deploy wait (the factory's deploy command): `bin/wait-dev-deploy [<sha>]`; rollback:
  `bin/wait-dev-deploy --rollback`
- Smoke test of a running instance: `bin/swagger_smoke http://localhost:3000`
  (`SMOKE_READ_ONLY=1` sends only GET requests, as prod does)
- Kamal configs (self-contained, always `-c`, never `-d`):
  `bundle exec kamal config -c config/deploy.dev.yml` (needs `DEV_HOST`, `KAMAL_REGISTRY_SERVER`),
  `bundle exec kamal config -c config/deploy.yml` (needs `PROD_VPN_IP`, `KAMAL_REGISTRY_SERVER`)
- Release tooling: `scripts/next-version.sh [<ref>]`, `scripts/release-notes.sh vX.Y.Z`, `bin/sdlc-metrics <tag>`,
  `bin/release prep|ship|rollback` (see "Automated release")

