## Branch model and releases

Short version; the rules are in `CLAUDE.md` ("Conventions", "Hard Rules").

- Features: `feature/<KEY>-<n>-<slug>` → squash PR into `develop` with title `<KEY>-<n>: <card title>` and exactly
  one `Type:` line in the body. `<KEY>` is `PROJECT_NAME` from `config/project.env` in capitals.
- Every commit on `develop` or `hotfix/*` that Rails Tests and Rails CI passed is deployed to dev by Dev Deploy.
- Release: a release-prep PR moves `[Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md` into `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`
  (`scripts/next-version.sh`), the release PR `develop` → `main`, titled `<KEY>-<n>: Release vX.Y.Z`, whose body has
  `## Changelog` with the version's CHANGELOG section (both PRs carry the release's own card, never `<KEY>-0`), is
  merged by hand with a merge commit, the operator tags the commit dev tested with an annotated `vX.Y.Z`, `Release`
  drafts the GitHub Release, and prod is deployed only from that tag:
  `gh workflow run "Kamal Deploy" --ref main -f environment=prod -f version=vX.Y.Z -f confirm=prod`.
  `release-watch` then watches `/health` and GlitchTip for 10 minutes; it never rolls back by itself.
- Rollback: `gh workflow run "Kamal Manage" --ref main -f action=rollback -f confirm=ROLLBACK-prod`.
- Hotfix: `hotfix/<KEY>-<n>-<slug>` from `main`, PR into `main` merged by hand, tagged with the PATCH version,
  then back-merged into `develop` with a merge commit.
- Published `v*` tags are never moved or deleted (`.githooks/pre-push`).

### Automated release (`bin/release`)

`bin/release` runs the flow above as one script, so the sdlc supervisor can release once every task of a feature
passed QA on dev; the manual steps stay valid. Every write goes through it, and `--dry-run` prints them as
`dry run: <command>` and runs only the read-only checks.

- `RELEASE_CARD=<KEY>-<n> bin/release prep`: the version is `scripts/next-version.sh origin/develop`, never typed.
  It moves the `[Unreleased]` entries into `## [X.Y.Z] - <today>` on `feature/<KEY>-<n>-release-X-Y-Z` and opens
  the release-prep PR `<KEY>-<n>: Release X.Y.Z changelog` (`Type: docs`) into `develop`; it does not merge it.
- `bin/release ship vX.Y.Z`, once that PR is merged: checks that `develop` is the release-prep commit D and that
  `scripts/next-version.sh` gives `X.Y.Z`, that the `RUNS_ON` variable pins a runner image (not `*latest*`), then
  `bin/wait-dev-deploy D` → release PR `<KEY>-<n>: Release vX.Y.Z` into `main` (checks green, merge commit) →
  annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` on D and its green `Release` run → with `RELEASE_MIRROR_REPO`, the mirror publish
  (`PUBLISH_MIRROR`, dry run first) → `Kamal Deploy` (`-f source_sha=D` on the mirror, `-f target=` the active
  prod target when the workflow takes one) and its `release-watch` → smoke: `/health` reports `release` D →
  e2e: `SMOKE_READ_ONLY=1 bin/swagger_smoke` against prod → the draft Release is published. Prints
  `shipped: vX.Y.Z D`.
- `bin/release rollback vX.Y.Z`: `Kamal Manage` rollback to that tag's commit, proven by `/health`. Nothing is
  deleted and no migration runs backwards.

A red (or failed dispatch of the) `Kamal Deploy` run, smoke or e2e prints `red: vX.Y.Z D <release-watch|smoke|e2e> <url>` and rolls back to
the previous release tag. When the release adds a migration under `db/migrate/` that the previous code cannot run
on (a contract step of `.claude/rules/migrations.md`: removing, renaming or retyping a column or table, also inside
`change_table`, raw SQL `DROP`/`RENAME`/`ALTER COLUMN` in a migration that calls `execute`, or
`IrreversibleMigration`), it prints `no auto-rollback: irreversible migration <files>` and rolls
nothing back: a person decides.

| Exit | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 0 | done (`prep: <KEY>-<n> X.Y.Z #<pr>`, `shipped: vX.Y.Z D`, `rolled back: vX.Y.Z <sha>`) |
| 1 | a precondition or a step before the prod deploy failed; prod untouched |
| 3 | red after the deploy; rolled back to the previous tag and `/health` proves it |
| 4 | red after the deploy and an irreversible migration: nothing rolled back, escalate |
| 5 | red after the deploy and the rollback did not verify (or no previous tag): escalate |
| 64 | usage |

Env: `RELEASE_MIRROR_REPO` (owner/name of the public mirror, default none), `PUBLISH_MIRROR` (default
`~/projects/mvp/1_mvp_sdlc/scripts/publish-mirror.sh`), `PROD_ACTIVE_TARGET` (`aws` or `srv`, default detected
from public DNS), `RELEASE_CHECKS_TIMEOUT` (1200 s), `RELEASE_POLL_INTERVAL` (30 s).

## Board flow

The project's Trello board has nine lists, in this order: `Backlog`, `Ready`, `In Progress`, `Review`, `Test`,
`Blocked`, `Ready to Release`, `Test after Release`, `Done`. The operator moves a card to `Ready` once the
Definition of Ready is met; from there the harness moves it (the factory to `In Progress`, `Review` and `Test`;
post-merge and the release runs onward); `Blocked` holds a card that waits for the operator or something
external. A renamed list goes under `trello.lists` in `.archon/factory-profile.yaml`. Who moves the card at each
step: [Board flow](https://github.com/OlegShevtsov1/1_mvp_sdlc/blob/{{SDLC_VERSION}}/docs/sdlc/03-dor-dod.md#board-flow).

## Beszel agent (prod host monitoring)

`config/deploy.yml` has the accessory `beszel-agent` (`henrygd/beszel-agent:0.21.0`, host network, listens on
45876, reachable only over the VPN). `kamal deploy` does not boot accessories, and the hub key is not a deploy
secret, so boot it once by hand from a console on the VPN with the deploy environment set:

```
BESZEL_HUB_KEY='<the hub public key>' PROD_VPN_IP=<prod VPN address> KAMAL_REGISTRY_SERVER=<registry> \
  bundle exec kamal accessory boot beszel-agent -c config/deploy.yml
```

`BESZEL_HUB_KEY` is the Beszel hub's public key (it contains a space, so quote it). Do not boot it on a host where
an agent already listens on 45876 (for example one deployed by the infrastructure repository): the second agent
cannot bind the port and would report the same host twice. The frontend shares the prod host and has no agent of
its own.

